# Deadly Precision with {4} payable and NOTHING to sacrifice (CR 601.2b): Bot1 controls only a Swamp, no artifact and no creature. Two Dark
# Rituals turn the Swamp's {B} into {B}{B}{B}{B}{B} in the pool (B -> BBB, then B of those -> BBB again: 5), which pays {B} plus {4}. The only
# way left to pay the additional cost is {4}, so no choice between the ways is asked (`! Bot1.Modes`), and Bot2's Llanowar Elves is destroyed. The
# other scenarios, in which a sacrifice is possible, ask the choice; deadly-precision-cannot-be-cast-with-no-artifact-or-creature-and-under-five-mana
# is the refusal when {4} is not payable either.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Dark Ritual
Dark Ritual
Deadly Precision
Island x3
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Forest x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Dark Ritual.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Mana = {B}{B}{B}
Bot1.Hand.Dark Ritual.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Mana = {B}{B}{B}{B}{B}
Bot1.Hand.Deadly Precision.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves)
! Bot1.Modes
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield = Swamp
Bot1.Graveyard = Deadly Precision; Dark Ritual; Dark Ritual
Bot2.Battlefield = Forest
Bot2.Graveyard = Llanowar Elves
